# Workspace Policy

## Supported AI Tools

This playbook supports four AI coding assistants. Each has its own discovery mechanism — there is no shared folder all of them read.

| AI Tool | Always-loaded instructions | Location |
|---|---|---|
| GitHub Copilot | `copilot-instructions.md` | `<repo-root>/.github/copilot-instructions.md` |
| Claude Code | `CLAUDE.md` | `<repo-root>/CLAUDE.md` |
| Cursor | `.mdc` rules (`alwaysApply: true`) | `<repo-root>/.cursor/rules/*.mdc` |
| OpenAI Codex CLI | `AGENTS.md` | `<repo-root>/AGENTS.md` (nearest wins for nested overrides) |

Run `/ai-tool-setup` to generate or refresh instruction files for all four tools.

## Rules, Commands, and Skills (Cursor)

As of Cursor 2.4 (January 2026), Cursor natively reads Agent Skills — the same open `SKILL.md` format used by Claude Code and Codex CLI — directly from `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (project) or `~/.cursor/skills/` (personal); it also reads the shared `.agents/skills/` location and, for legacy compatibility, `.claude/skills/` and `.codex/skills/`. All three Cursor mechanisms coexist and serve different purposes:

| Mechanism | Location | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| Rules | `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` | Short, always-on or glob-scoped guidance auto-attached by file type (like this document) |
| Commands | `.cursor/commands/*.md` | Simple one-off actions invoked explicitly with `/name` |
| Skills | `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` | Longer, multi-step procedures — explicitly invoked with `/name` or model-selected from `name`/`description`, optionally scoped to file types via a `paths` frontmatter field, and able to bundle `scripts/`, `references/`, and `assets/` subfolders |

This playbook's 13 procedures (the 6 skills and 7 former-agents under `.claude/skills/` and `.claude/agents/`) are ported to Cursor as native skills under `.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. The routing table below points at those files. The existing `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` file-type rules and `.cursor/commands/*.md` commands remain valid and continue to work — this is additive, not a replacement.

